From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: cpu_features: hwcap bits as unsigned long long

AARCH64_HWCAP2_* above bit 31 are (1UL << n). Where long is 32 bits
(AArch64 ILP32) the shift overflows and the hwcaps table initializers are
not constant. With 1ULL the values are the same on LP64; on ILP32 they
become 0 in the unsigned long table, i.e. not detected (IsSet compares 32
bits anyway).

